---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: docs-plans-legacy-routing
purpose: "Legacy/parallel plans dir (stalled since May). New plans belong in genesis/docs/superpowers/plans/ where the gate lives."
rules:
  - id: route-plans-to-governed-home
    class: dispatch
    when: { write: "*.md", new: true }
    route-to: { dest: genesis/docs/superpowers/plans/ }
    parameters:
      dispatch-agent: librarian
      dispatch-prompt: >
        Confirm whether this is genuinely a new plan and name the governed destination or an
        existing artifact to merge into. Report ROUTE, MERGE, or DROP to the editing agent; do not
        move or create files and do not derail implementation.
    why: "New plans go to genesis/docs/superpowers/plans/ (governed) — not this stalled legacy dir."
---
# docs/plans (legacy)

The active plans home is `genesis/docs/superpowers/plans/` (governed by the lifecycle gate). This legacy
dir stalled in May; new plans are routed there at birth so they land under governance. Existing files
are left in place.
